<%# locals: (form:, attribute:, choices:, selected:, labelled_by:, input_data: {}, hints: {}) %>
<%#
  "Pick one of N" as real radios in labelled cards. The chosen card is styled
  from the input's own state (.choice-card:has(> input:checked)), so there is no
  controller keeping a hidden field and a class in step. Each radio posts as
  step[<attribute>] and autosaves on change; a caller's own action runs first,
  so it can stopImmediatePropagation() to veto the save (question-form does).

  `hints` is an optional { value => short marker } map. A control may arrive
  with NOTHING selected: a Question silently defaulted to "Text
  Input" runs and is wrong, which is far harder to notice than one that is
  obviously unset — and WorkflowHealthCheck now reports the unset case. The
  marker exists so "pick one" is still steered rather than left blank, which is
  how Zingtree labels its own most-used node type. A builder-made Question is
  the exception — GrowStep starts it as Yes / No.
%>
<% hints ||= {} %>
<% data = input_data.merge(action: [input_data[:action], "change->inline-autosave#schedule"].compact.join(" ")) %>
<div class="choice-cards" role="radiogroup" aria-labelledby="<%= labelled_by %>">
  <% choices.each do |label, value| %>
    <label class="choice-card">
      <%= form.radio_button attribute, value, checked: selected == value, class: "sr-only", data: data %>
      <span><%= label %></span>
      <% if hints[value].present? %>
        <span class="choice-card__hint"><%= hints[value] %></span>
      <% end %>
    </label>
  <% end %>
</div>
